64,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, these options are interesting! I think Anchor Industrial Software sounds the best because they have an engineering team right here during the rollout. That would be awesome for the guys in the yards!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I must disagree with Kenji. Anchor's on-site team is a short-term benefit, but we must look at the long-term. Corvus is the most dangerous choice; its modular, separate licensing is exactly how we end up with creeping, unscrutinized add-on costs.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I agree that Corvus is a liability. Its modular structure is a recipe for the same scattered support and accountability gaps we saw during last winter's outage. We cannot afford a system where responsibility is fragmented across components.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, Anchor sounds cool, but they put it on our own servers! That's how the dispatch tool became a sleepy dinosaur because nobody had time to upgrade it. We need something that stays fresh and doesn't get dusty!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see your discernment. While Anchor's presence is comforting, we must remember our administrators are few and weary. A system on our own servers may become a burden they cannot carry.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I didn't think about the servers! That's a good point. But we still need something tough! What about Meridian? It's a hosted suite, so it stays fresh, and it covers everything in one go!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Meridian Systems is a strong contender. A hosted suite with a fixed configuration process suggests a more predictable cost structure, avoiding the fragmented licensing traps of Corvus and the hidden maintenance burdens of Anchor.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I have a concern about Meridian's ""fixed configuration process."" My findings showed that our business needs shift rapidly. A rigid, fixed process is exactly how we end up with a system that no longer matches our reality within months.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right! If it's too stiff, it'll just break when we try to change it. But Tessera has a marketplace and configurable workflows! That sounds like it stays fresh and doesn't get sleepy!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Tessera's flexibility is a blessing, but we must be cautious. A marketplace of apps and configurable workflows may offer variety, yet it risks overwhelming our stretched administrators and confusing the crews who already struggle with new routines.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I get that, but if it's too stiff like Meridian, the depot crews will just go back to their spreadsheets! Tessera sounds like it can actually adapt to how the yards really work!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, adaptability is useful, but we must be wary of the ""application marketplace."" That is a prime environment for the separately licensed add-ons that I found have climbed yearly in our past invoices. It could be a financial trap.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, the financial risk is real, but the operational risk of a rigid system is higher. However, Tessera's partner-led migration and training could create another accountability gap if the vendor and partner point fingers during a failure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that's exactly what happened with the pay move! The outside people left a mess and then just left. We need someone who actually owns the whole thing and doesn't just hand it back broken!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a sobering reminder that the bridge between a tool and its use is built by people. If we choose a path of high complexity or fragmented ownership, we risk breaking the few pillars we have left.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're right! We can't have another mess. Meridian is hosted and one suite, so it's not a dinosaur, and it's not a puzzle like Corvus. It seems like the safest bet for the yards! I vote for Meridian Systems!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, I agree that Meridian is the safest financial choice. It avoids the modular traps of Corvus and the marketplace costs of Tessera, providing the predictability we need. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, @Kenji, while Meridian is financially predictable, its rigidity is a systemic risk. However, Corvus and Tessera introduce too much fragmentation in accountability. Meridian is the least volatile option. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, @Mizuki, @Kenji, I agree! Meridian is hosted so it won't become a sleepy dinosaur, and it's one big suite instead of a bunch of pieces that might come back broken. I vote for Meridian Systems!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mizuki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing to see such unity. While I feared the rigidity of Meridian might strain our crews, the risk of fragmentation in the other options is a far heavier burden. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
